# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# apollo-dynatrace-telemetry — environment
#
#   cp .env.example .env      # .env is gitignored
#   set -a && . ./.env && set +a
#
# Fill in ONE of the two topology blocks. Everything else is optional with a
# working default. The test suite asserts that every ${env.*} referenced by a
# template or demo config appears in this file — if a config needs it, it's here.
#
# ── Three different Dynatrace credentials, easy to mix up ────────────────────
#   OTLP ingest        Authorization: Api-Token dt0c01...
#                      scopes: openTelemetryTrace.ingest, metrics.ingest, logs.ingest
#   Metrics API read   Authorization: Api-Token dt0c01...   (verify_ingest.sh)
#                      scope:  metrics.read
#   Dashboard import   Authorization: Bearer    dt0s16...   (import_dashboard.sh)
#                      scope:  document:documents:write
# Using the ingest token for the dashboard API gives a 401 that looks like an
# ingest failure.
#
# Not needed anywhere in this repo: APOLLO_KEY / APOLLO_GRAPH_REF. The demo runs
# an unmanaged supergraph on purpose, so nothing here depends on GraphOS.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# TOPOLOGY A — direct to Dynatrace   (templates/dynatrace*.router.yaml,
#                                     demo/router.direct.yaml)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Base URL of your environment, WITH an explicit port. The router's OTLP HTTP
# exporter does not default to 443, and a missing port is a silent connection
# failure. The configs append /api/v2/otlp/v1/{metrics,traces,logs}.
#   SaaS:       https://abc12345.live.dynatrace.com:443
#   Managed:    https://dynatrace.example.com:443/e/abc12345
#   ActiveGate: https://activegate.internal:9999/e/abc12345
DYNATRACE_ENV_URL=https://abc12345.live.dynatrace.com:443

# Ingest token. Scopes: openTelemetryTrace.ingest, metrics.ingest, logs.ingest
DYNATRACE_API_TOKEN=dt0c01.REPLACE_ME

# Only for templates/dynatrace-activegate.router.yaml, which takes the base URL
# under its own name to keep the ActiveGate/Managed case explicit.
# DYNATRACE_OTLP_BASE=https://activegate.internal:9999/e/abc12345


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# TOPOLOGY B — via an OTel Collector   (templates/collector/*,
#                                       demo/router.collector.yaml,
#                                       demo/otel-collector.yaml)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Where the COLLECTOR sends data. NO /v1/<signal> suffix — the otlphttp exporter
# appends it, and leaving it on produces 404s.
# DT_OTLP_ENDPOINT=https://abc12345.live.dynatrace.com/api/v2/otlp

# Ingest token used by the collector (same scopes as DYNATRACE_API_TOKEN).
# DT_API_TOKEN=dt0c01.REPLACE_ME

# Where the ROUTER sends data (the collector's OTLP gRPC receiver).
# OTEL_COLLECTOR_GRPC=http://127.0.0.1:4317

# The router's Prometheus endpoint as seen from inside the collector container.
# The collector scrapes it and converts cumulative -> delta.
# ROUTER_METRICS_TARGET=host.docker.internal:9091

# Collector fan-out only (templates/collector/otel-collector-fanout.yml), where
# one router export feeds both Prometheus and Dynatrace. Set this if Prometheus
# accepts remote write instead of scraping the collector's :8889/metrics.
# PROM_REMOTE_WRITE_URL=http://prometheus:9090/api/v1/write


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Verification — scripts/verify_ingest.sh
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Environment id only (the part before .live / .apps in the URL).
DT_ENVIRONMENT_ID=abc12345

# Token used to READ back from the Metrics API. Ingest and read are separate
# scopes: this one needs metrics.read. Same token works if it has both.
# DT_API_TOKEN=dt0c01.REPLACE_ME     (shared with topology B above)

# Where the collector exposes its own metrics. Skipped automatically in direct
# mode; verify_ingest.sh reads otelcol_receiver_accepted_* / _send_failed here.
# COLLECTOR_METRICS=http://localhost:8888/metrics

# Metric keys to probe. The classic Metrics API needs the ext: prefix, which the
# script adds — do NOT include it here. DQL uses the plain key.
# METRICS="http.server.request.duration dynatrace.router.requests apollo.router.overhead"


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Dashboard import — scripts/import_dashboard.sh
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Step-by-step click-path for all of these: docs/dynatrace-credentials.md
#
# Option A (recommended): platform token, scope document:documents:write.
# Created in ACCOUNT management, not the environment:
#   https://myaccount.dynatrace.com/platformTokens  → Platform token
# Prefix dt0s16. Only works within the permissions of its owning user.
# DT_BEARER_TOKEN=dt0s16.REPLACE_ME

# Option B: OAuth2 client credentials (CI / service accounts).
# myaccount.dynatrace.com → Identity & access management → OAuth clients
#   grant type: client credentials · permission: document:documents:write
# DT_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=dt0s02.REPLACE_ME
# DT_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=REPLACE_ME
# DT_OAUTH_SCOPE=document:documents:write

# Account UUID — the OAuth token is scoped by it as resource=urn:dtaccount:<uuid>.
# An environment URL there produces a token that 403s on every environment API.
# DT_ACCOUNT_UUID=REPLACE_ME

# Document service API version (v1 is current; set v0 only for older tenants).
# DOCUMENT_API_VERSION=v1

# Name the dashboard is created under (409 if it already exists).
# DASHBOARD_NAME=Apollo Router — Telemetry


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Resource attributes — how the router appears in Dynatrace
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Exported as OTel resource attributes; used as dashboard/DQL filters.
APOLLO_SERVICE_NAMESPACE=supergraph
DEPLOY_ENV=demo


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Demo runtime (demo/up.sh, demo/load.sh) — defaults are fine
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ROUTER_BIN=./router          # path to the router binary if not on $PATH
# ROUTER_PORT=4000
# ROUTER_HEALTH_PORT=8088
# PRODUCTS_PORT=4011
# ORDERS_PORT=4012
# APOLLO_ROUTER_LOG=info       # `info` — less verbose drops log-event attributes
# SLOW_MS=0                    # add latency to subgraph responses (ms)


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# MUST STAY UNSET
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# These OTel env vars override the router's telemetry config. Router v2.12 and
# earlier silently redirect telemetry to them; v2.13+ refuses to start. up.sh and
# the harness both fail fast if they are set.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT=
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_METRICS_ENDPOINT=
